  with.

  [1mBehavior[0m, given [38;5;153mmaxLength = options.truncate[39m and the ellipsis inside the budget:

  ┌────────────────────────┬──────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │         Input          │ [38;5;153mtruncate[39m │                      Output                       │
  ├────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153m"hello"[39m                │ [38;5;153m10[39m       │ [38;5;153m"hello"[39m — under the limit, untouched, no ellipsis │
  ├────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153m"hello world"[39m          │ [38;5;153m8[39m        │ [38;5;153m"hello..."[39m — cut back to the space                │
  ├────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153m"supercalifragilistic"[39m │ [38;5;153m8[39m        │ [38;5;153m"super..."[39m — no space in budget, hard cut         │
  ├────────────────────────┼──────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ [38;5;153m"hello world"[39m          │ [38;5;153m2[39m        │ [38;5;153m".."[39m — budget below the ellipsis itself           │
  └────────────────────────┴──────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Trailing whitespace is trimmed before [38;5;153m'...'[39m is appended, so you never get [38;5;153m"hello ..."[39m.

  [1mPlacement in the pipeline[0m — this is the one decision I'd flag. I'd put the truncate block after [38;5;153muppercase[39m/[38;5;153mlowercase[39m
  but [1mbefore[0m [38;5;153mprefix[39m/[38;5;153msuffix[39m, so [38;5;153mmaxLength[39m bounds the string being formatted rather than the assembled result. The
  alternative (truncate last) would honor "output never exceeds maxLength" literally, but it would silently chop off a
  [38;5;153msuffix[39m the caller explicitly asked for, which is worse. Consequence to accept: with a prefix or suffix present, the
  returned string can exceed [38;5;153mmaxLength[39m. Say the word if you'd rather have the literal guarantee.

